after months of sneak peeks and teases  Disney has finally released the first  official trailer for its live adaptation  of Aladdin we're again greeted by a few  familiar faces as well as several new  things we've not seen from the 1992  original here's everything you need to  know about the new trailer for a ladder  the new trailer is chock-full of moments  that will make you reminisce about the  original animation  it begins with Aladdin's first  introduction as he's chased by three  city guards across the city through the  streets and over the roof in the  original it was for stealing a loaf of  bread which he carries prominently  throughout the chase giving us a few  comedic moments like this one but it's  clearly missing from the movies so why  is Aladdin being chased something else  that seems to be missing from the scene  is one of the very first scores of  Aladdin one jump ahead which really  introduces Aladdin as a character along  with his backstory from the rest of the  trailer it's clear we'll definitely see  some of the original musical scores so  could this possibly mean that we might  not get all the musical numbers from the  original in the film we also get a more  comprehensive look at the familiar faces  from the original we see Rajah Jasmine's  pet tiger once again walking  majestically down the steps along with  jasmine but for a split second we also  see him protecting jasmine from the  palace cons probably after Jafar has  taken over the Empire with genies help  we also see the magic carpet in action  helping Aladdin multiple times from  danger and also in this iconic scene but  more on that later  Yago Jafar's parrot that we've seen  flying from behind in every single  trailer finally makes his front sight  debut and he's huge most likely from  Jafar's magic chasing Aladdin and Abu  across the city and of course Genie who  was the center of controversy after his  first appearance we definitely see more  of genies charm  and wit's in this trailer as well as  some of the incredible magic he performs  and speaking of genie it's impossible  not to go over the masterful original  scores that make a reappearance in the  film like Will Smith performing friend  like me with the same magical visuals  from the original and of course one of  the most memorable musical numbers in  all of Disney's animation a whole new  world and although we don't get to hear  it it's obvious that we'll see a  performance of Prince Ali here is  Aladdin disguised as a prince makes his  return to the city without a doubt the  new adaptation of Aladdin is aware and  reminiscent of its predecessor just like  all of Disney's recent live adaptations  but that doesn't mean Disney hasn't  taken any creative liberties and some  are a little more worrisome than others  the choice to magically enlarge Iago for  an epic chase scene makes sense  films director Guy Ritchie is known for  his stylish visuals and epic set pieces  but the decision to let genie have a  human form is questionable sure it lets  us know that it's Will Smith who is the  only recognizable face in a cast full of  newcomers but it doesn't make much sense  other than showing Will Smith as himself  on screen not to mention it will make  Aladdin fring genie feel much less  impactful the same goes for the scene  where Jafar brings Aladdin to the Cave  of Wonders  but as himself unlike the original where  he disguised himself as an old man to  trick Aladdin it's a subtle yet  important plot point in the original  that really gives us an idea of what  kind of a man Jafar really is without  subtle moments like this it's possible  that your farm might be another flat  villain simply there to progress the  story Disney's live adaptations have  been most successful when they merge the  traditions of the original with  forward-thinking changes it's a tricky  balance and the changes we've witness  so far and the trailer are worrisome to  say the least so what did you think  about the trailer what are you most  excited about are you okay with the  creative liberties they took with a  story and is Jeannie still creepy tell  us in the comments below
 

